-- ============================================================
-- Migration 010: TC Questionnaire Rebuild
-- Full path: thyroconsult-backend\migrations\010_tc_questionnaire_rebuild.sql
--
-- PROBLEM: TcQuestionnaire.js (the live frontend component) uses 216
-- distinct data fields, plus ~73 more generated by shared helper
-- functions (renderLabScreen/renderSymptomScreen/renderMultiSymptom/
-- renderComorbidity) using template-literal keys. Of all fields the
-- component actually reads/writes, only a handful matched the live
-- tc_questionnaire table (built in migration 002 for a different,
-- snapshot-at-diagnosis data model: tsh_at_diagnosis, tg_at_diagnosis, etc).
--
-- This migration adds every column the live component needs to save
-- correctly, matching field names and types exactly against the code.
-- It does NOT drop the old snapshot-style columns (mtc_*, *_at_diagnosis,
-- t_stage/n_stage/m_stage/overall_stage/risk_category, surveillance_interval,
-- next_tg_date etc.) since dropping columns on a live table needs a
-- separate, deliberate decision once you've confirmed nothing reads them.
--
-- Run once in pgAdmin on the thyroconsult database as superuser
-- All statements use IF NOT EXISTS — safe to re-run
-- Run AFTER migration 009 (which already added Module B + marital_status)
-- ============================================================

